[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115015,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Osteochondroma is a benign neoplasm forming a bony projection with a cartilaginous cap, with continuity between the marrow cavity of the tumour and underlying bone.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:33:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115016,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9210/0 Osteochondroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:33:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115017,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E83.Y &amp; XH5Y87 Benign osteogenic tumour of other specified site &amp; Osteochondroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:33:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115018,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> osteochondromatous exostosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:33:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115019,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:33:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115020,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Osteochondromas are rare in the craniofacial bones, usually involving the mandibular condyle and coronoid process {22727110}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:33:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115021,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Craniofacial osteochondromas often cause swelling, asymmetry, trismus, and temporomandibular joint dysfunction {21367506; 22727110}, but they may be chance radiographic findings. Osteochondromas may be multiple, but multiple lesions usually affect long bones.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Radiographic imaging shows an uneven enlargement or protrusion from the condyle {22727110; 28110943}, unlike the diffuse condylar enlargement of condylar hyperplasia.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:33:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115022,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Osteochondroma of the jaw manifests in the second to fourth decades of life, slightly later than at other sites, and unlike at other sites it often continues to grow slowly after puberty {7629631}. A slight female predominance is seen {21367506}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:33:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115023,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Trauma and (rarely) prior radiotherapy may be etiological factors {21367506}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:33:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115024,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "<p>Homozygous deletions of <em>EXT1</em> are associated with sporadic osteochondromas, suggesting a neoplastic rather than developmental condition {33622860}. Heterozygous germline mutations of <em>EXT1</em> and <em>EXT2</em> are associated with hereditary multiple osteochondroma, but the facial bones are not usually affected {18271966; 33622860}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-01-10T12:46:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115025,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Osteochondroma is a bony mass, sessile or pedunculated, with a cartilage cap.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:33:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115026,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Osteochondroma is a cartilage-capped bony projection from the external bone surface, showing cortical and medullary continuity with the parent bone. There is a surface layer of fibrous tissue and a middle layer that mimics growth plate cartilage with endochondral ossification, merging with underlying mature trabecular bone {28110943; 31842965}. Binucleated cells, nodularity, and cystic/mucoid changes may be present, but neither mitoses nor marked pleomorphism are seen {22555180}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Although a cartilaginous cap &gt;&nbsp;20&nbsp;mm in thickness in adults must raise the suspicion of secondary chondrosarcoma, occurrence in the facial bones is very rare {33622860}. Criteria for the histological distinction of osteochondroma from condylar hyperplasia are poorly defined {28110943; 31842965}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:33:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115027,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:33:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115028,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:33:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115029,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> pedunculated or broad-based bony exostosis; a cartilaginous cap with a growth plate&ndash;like architecture; continuity with underlying bone cortex and marrow.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:33:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115030,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:33:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115031,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Recurrence after excision is rare, unless the lesion is incompletely removed {22727110; 33622860}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:33:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]